{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1579,
    "dDurationMs": 5001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gasoline has approximately 56 Megajoules of\nchemical energy per liter , which is more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6580,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy than you get from exploding the same\nof amount of TNT, and is enough to power a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10170,
    "dDurationMs": 2139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "toaster for a full day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12309,
    "dDurationMs": 4101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cars work by burning gasoline to convert that\nchemical energy into the kinetic energy of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16410,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "motion of the car, though almost 80% of it\nis lost as heat in the engine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20710,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, 20% of 56 million joules is a lot of\njoules…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25000,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To give a direct sense of gas-to-car conversion,\nit takes about five teaspoons of of gas to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30070,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accelerate a 2 ton car to 60kph, and about\na third of a cup more for every additional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35330,
    "dDurationMs": 2399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minute you want to keep it going at that speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37729,
    "dDurationMs": 4781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That might not sound like a lot of fuel, but\nthe energy of a car moving 60kph is equivalent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42510,
    "dDurationMs": 4719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to dropping an elephant – or stegosaurus\n– from the top of a three-story building."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47229,
    "dDurationMs": 3151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in order for the car to stop, all that\nenergy has to go somewhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50380,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the brakes do the stopping, they dissipate\nthe energy by heating up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54540,
    "dDurationMs": 3730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the case of a collision, energy is dissipated\nby the bending and crumpling of metal in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58270,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outer areas of the car."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59900,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just like how smooth braking is nicer\nthan a quick jerky stop, cars are carefully"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64180,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "designed to crumple - when they crash - in\na way that lengthens the duration of the impact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that stopping requires less intense acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lots of acceleration over a very short time\nis not good for soft human brains and organs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77280,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, people don’t like driving cars\nwith Pinocchio-length noses, so most cars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81960,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only have around 50 cm of crushable space\nin which to dissipate the energy equivalent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86500,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our falling stegosaur."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88130,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means that, while crumpling, they need\nto maintain a resistive force of about a quarter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92320,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the thrust of the space shuttle main engine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94880,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over half of the controlled-crumpling work\nis done by a pair of steel rails connecting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98670,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the front bumper to the body, which bend and\ndeform to absorb energy and slow the car."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103560,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of the rest of the energy is absorbed\nby the deformation of other pieces of structural"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108950,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "metal throughout the front of the car."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110690,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This meticulously engineered destruction allows\na crashing car to decelerate at a high but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115190,
    "dDurationMs": 5590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reasonable rate: just slightly over the acceleration\nexperienced by fighter pilots or astronauts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120780,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in centrifuge training."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122270,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As comparison, if cars were super rigid (like\nthey were before the 1950s) and didn’t crumple,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127320,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would stop so fast that they would undergo\nacceleration 15 times what fighter pilots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131920,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experience in training."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135629,
    "dDurationMs": 3951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thankfully engineers have learned to make\ncars with crunchy crumple zones surrounding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139580,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their rigid safety cell, because fully rigid\ncars are not good for fighter pilots or anyone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144510,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145560,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except, maybe, robots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148730,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This MinutePhysics video was made possible\nby Ford - I was able to talk to an awesome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152520,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crash test safety engineer there who told\nme all about the complex physics and engineering"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156590,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that goes into vehicle development and improving\nhow cars perform in a crash."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160740,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ford gave me this opportunity because they\nwant you to know how important and carefully"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163730,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "designed all the parts involved are, and in\nparticular that the only parts developed and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167610,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tested to work with their vehicles are original\nFord parts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170370,
    "dDurationMs": 5089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to learn more about why the right\nparts matter, you can head to takeagoodlook.com."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175459,
    "dDurationMs": 3611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I personally want to say that making this\nvideo has just reinforced to me that regardless"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179070,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of what kind of car you have, big dents and\ndeformations in the body aren’t just aesthetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183230,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "problems – they can be safety hazards, too."
    } ]
  } ]
}
